No files, branches, environments, datasets, or simulations were modified. This was a read-only investigation.

## 1. Executive Summary

**Recommended strategy:** create `feature/benchmark-integration` from **`origin/predicate-guide`**, but isolate benchmark adapters from the existing research-stage runtime. Start with dataset extraction, then GOAT/Habitat integration, then SOON/MatterSim integration.

NeuroNav has a vendored C++/ROS 2 Hydra stack plus Python runtime adapters. `predicate-guide` adds a Habitat ROS bridge, world-snapshot representation, frontier scoring, and predicate-stage experiments. It is the strongest code base, but it does **not** prove an end-to-end GOAT or SOON pipeline works.

The least-risk path is:

```text
official annotations → lossless JSONL extraction
GOAT Habitat episode → RGB-D/pose/semantic adapter → Hydra → DSG snapshot
DSG snapshot + task metadata → predicate scorer → candidate/action adapter
SOON MatterSim viewpoint graph → discrete candidate/action adapter
```

