**Supported by official documentation:** GOAT uses Habitat-Sim `0.2.3`, Habitat-Lab `v0.2.3`, Python `3.7` in its documented environment; uses HM3D assets and splits `train`, `val_seen`, `val_seen_synonyms`, `val_unseen`; official evaluation invokes `python -um goat_bench.run --run-type eval`. [GOAT README](https://github.com/Ram81/goat-bench/blob/main/README.md)

GOAT is the better first simulator target because NeuroNav already has a Habitat-Sim worker, MP3D-style RGB-D bridge, TF convention, and Hydra launch. It still needs an episode-aware replacement or extension of the current random-start Habitat worker.

GOAT’s task sequence may contain category, language, and image goals. Only original language fields should become description records; category-only/image-only subtasks must remain explicitly non-linguistic.

## 8. SOON Feasibility

| Component | Assessment |
|---|---|
| Dataset access | Adapter required |
| Task extraction | Adapter required |
| RGB | Adapter required |
| Depth | Adapter required |
| Camera poses | Adapter required |
