| Closed-loop exploration | Major modification |
| Official evaluation | Adapter required |

**Supported by official documentation:** FAO provides `train.json`, `val_unseen_instrs.json`, `val_unseen_house.json`, and `test.json`. [Official SOON page](https://scenario-oriented-object-navigation.github.io/)

MatterSim is viewpoint-graph navigation, not continuous navigation:

- state includes a scan ID, viewpoint and navigable neighbors;
- actions select a neighbor index and alter heading/elevation;
- RGB is available; depth exists only when enabled and uses z-depth, with raw values divided by 4000 for metres;
- viewpoints are sparse, on average about 2.25 m apart;
- camera heading/elevation can change at a viewpoint.

[Official Matterport3D Simulator README](https://github.com/peteanderson80/Matterport3DSimulator/blob/master/README.md)

The graph is normally exposed through `navigableLocations`; whether it is “known” to the policy depends on what the adapter reveals. Do not expose complete connectivity if evaluating under an unknown-environment assumption.

### SOON action options

| Option | Change effort | Fidelity to predicate exploration |
|---|---|---|
| A. Score valid MatterSim viewpoints directly | Lower | Lower; replaces continuous frontiers with sparse graph nodes |
| B. Select Hydra frontier, project/snap to reachable viewpoints | Higher | Higher, but fragile |

Recommendation: begin with **A** for a valid runnable prototype. Move to **B** only after establishing depth/pose reconstruction and reachability projection.

### Continuous SOON in Habitat

| Requirement | Original SOON + MatterSim | Adapted SOON + Habitat |
|---|---|---|
| Official compatibility | Verified | Not official |
| Hydra compatibility | Major modification | Adapter required |
| Geometric exploration | Sparse viewpoints | Stronger continuous support |
| Implementation complexity | Lower for official scoring | Lower for Hydra, higher for benchmark fidelity |
| Evaluation comparability | Official | Requires a separately declared protocol |

Using the same MP3D scenes in Habitat does not reproduce SOON: start viewpoints, discrete transitions, rendered observations, target localization, and official success conditions all need redefinition or exact conversion. This is a **reasonable inference**, not verified equivalence.

## 9. Dataset Extraction Plan

Extraction does not require either simulator once official annotation files are available.

Suggested lossless JSONL schema:

```json
{
  "benchmark": "goat|soon",
  "split": "official split name",
  "source_file": "relative original annotation path",
  "source_record_index": 0,
  "episode_id": "original value or null",
  "subtask_id": "original value or null",
  "subtask_index": 0,
  "scene_id": "original value or null",
  "goal_type": "language|category|image|unknown",
  "description_original": "verbatim string or null",
  "description_components_original": {},
  "start": {"position": null, "rotation": null, "viewpoint_id": null, "heading": null},
  "target_metadata_official": {},
  "ground_truth_official": {},
  "derived": {}
}
```

Rules:

- Store every source string byte-for-byte after JSON decoding; never normalize, translate, merge, or paraphrase.
- Emit one row per GOAT sequential subtask and retain its sequence index.
- Preserve SOON components separately if source JSON has separate object/relationship/region/nearby-region fields; retain any original combined description independently.
- Use `null` for unavailable data; never synthesize descriptions for image/category goals.
- Preserve whole official target structures under `target_metadata_official`.
- Validate: source-row count, unique key `(benchmark, split, episode_id, subtask_id/index)`, exact raw-string round trip, source-file provenance, and split totals.

**Unknown:** exact GOAT and SOON JSON field names must be established by inspecting the downloaded official annotations. Neither dataset is locally available in this worktree.

