## 13. Technical Risks

1. **High — SOON discrete vs. Hydra continuous geometry.** Begin with graph-node candidates; document loss of continuous-frontier behavior.
2. **High — official benchmark validity.** A Habitat port of SOON is a new protocol, not official SOON.
3. **High — semantic representation.** GOAT/SOON language is richer than the current manually fixed chair/table relation protocol.
4. **Medium — simulator dependency conflicts.** GOAT’s documented Habitat 0.2.3/Python 3.7 differs from NeuroNav’s checked-in Habitat environment specifying Python 3.9.
5. **Medium — coordinate/depth calibration.** Prove pixel-depth-to-world consistency before mapping claims.
6. **Medium — existing experiment maturity.** Existing launch/script presence is not end-to-end validation.

